hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-39 : List (List Word)
hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-39 = cons "Today's knowledge graphs model the world and leave out the work that produces and uses knowledge. In hyperactivity" (cons "the task graph (lib/task-graph.cub) is a graph of the same kind. A node is a goal named by an English sentence; it" (cons "exists because of what it serves (its parts-of list); and it is resolved when its children are. Once" (cons "knowledge-work intentions go into this graph (a publication to write, a field's ignorance to dispel), the workflow" (cons "graph and the knowledge graph are one graph. The workflow is the record of work done, work pending, and what serves" (cons "what. Everything written is work done: code for some interpreter, serving some purpose. A document is a projection" (cons "of values, computed whenever it is read, so it can't be stale. The paper itself exists once, as a value, with its" (cons "human and pure presentations as projections." (cons "" nil))))))))
